geogcomments:
coordinate based on Laguna Paraguaya
The findings were made at two different points, namely: a wide arid depression, to the SE. of the Epecuén lagoon, whose waters must have invaded it more than once, and which forms part of the field of the Robillote Succession, between the lagoon and the town of Alsina; 
and the bed, at the time almost entirely dry, of the Laguna de Los Paraguayos "to the N. of the town) about a league to the E. of the Laguna de Epecuén.

